# THE WOOD'S NEW WAYS WEST (2026-11-22), built with the cave under the wood.
#
# Every way from a gate to the western wood ran through three rooms: the Moss
# Floor, the Clay Shelf and the Leaning Limes. All the cave's ways in are west of
# them, so three people could shut the cave and the western wood off from the
# world. The throat check found it; this file opens the wood until the narrowest
# point between the gates and the cave is the cave's own six mouths (six ways
# in for 238 rooms behind them: the rule's one per 40).
#
# Picked by max-flow from every door the map allows, leaving out the ground
# built closed on purpose: the-wood-4.rooms (the far side, the holding, cores G
# and H) and the bear caves. Every door joins two rooms already side by side on
# the map, and the new rooms stand on squares nobody held.
#
# It also keeps the cave's rule that every way into the cave is at least 14
# steps from every other: doors that would bring two of them closer (the
# Spring Mire to the Deer Fence, the Crows' Oak to the Deep Roots, the Ferny
# Bank to the Stone Oak) were tried and left out.
#
#   FIVE DOORS between old rooms:
#     the Pine Dark - the Murk            the Black Alders - the Alder Stand
#     the Sapling Crowd - the Buckled Ground
#     the Wild Cherry - the Deep Roots    the Boundary Cross - the Pay Stone
#   UNDER THE DEEP ROOTS: three rooms from the Soft Floor round behind the wall
#     of roots, so the Ferny Bank's ground has a second way in.
#   THE OLD GROWTH'S NORTH WAY: two rooms off the Mounting Block, the Cut Line
#     and the Tally Posts. They used to go on west into the Bounds House, one
#     room from the Heart of It, and that put the woodward nine steps from the
#     Gate Arch where the maze had kept him forty-two; the door is gone (mig
#     413, 2026-11-25). The old growth still has four ways in without it.
#   THE GATEHOUSE ROAD: twelve rooms from the Rampart Walk down to the Frog
#     Chorus, so the Ward Ditch (the sixth way into the cave) has a way in that
#     is not the Killing Ground. It comes in the long way round on purpose: the
#     short way would put the ditch five steps from the Gate Arch.
!region wood

## the-pine-dark | attachment: the rows run on south into the murk
!existing
> south the-murk

## the-murk | attachment
!existing
> north the-pine-dark

